WEBVTT

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:12.050
As a result of space development, the waste, Space Debris, is actually a very dangerous existence.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:19.500
This is the story of the era when space garbage became a problem in 2075.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.480
The net profit is 15% growth.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.590
This year, the second business department is the top.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.710
Even the second business department has a red paper office.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:30.710
Is it half price?

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:31.350
Yes.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.400
Ah, excuse me.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:35.560
Debris.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.560
As you know, the cost of collecting debris is paid according to the number of points determined by the Federation.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.720
But in the end, it's just a number of points.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.740
It doesn't necessarily have the number of points that match the cost.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.630
In other words, to make it black, you need to get a high number of points from the Federation.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:54.120
But...

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.560
That's why.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:58.310
Claire-kun, can you ask me one thing?

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.260
What is it?

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:38.940
I'm sorry.

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:01.570
See you next time.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.440
You copy the target object?

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.120
I copy.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:38.660
Zoom.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:39.400
I copy.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.670
Hit confirmed.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.400
Target changed. Your light.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:43.820
Copy.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:49.530
Come on, you're going to say anything!

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.840
I told you to keep it simple!

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.310
You got it, Siri?

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:56.680
Please stop with that Siri thing!

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.980
After you get here, you're going to-

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.700
It's already been a month.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.060
It's still a month.

00:03:03.452 --> 00:03:06.752
Then, how many months will it take for you to call me by my name?

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:09.532
Hey, this is a hair spray, right?

00:03:09.628 --> 00:03:12.988
I forgot. It's all because of the weightlessness.

00:03:12.988 --> 00:03:14.088
Who are you?

00:03:14.088 --> 00:03:15.828
Wow, cheap stuff.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:16.428
Hey!

00:03:16.448 --> 00:03:17.748
Who are you talking to?

00:03:18.012 --> 00:03:22.292
When you ask someone's name, don't you learn it from yourself first?

00:03:22.684 --> 00:03:23.544
Maia?

00:03:23.772 --> 00:03:25.532
I'm Corinne Clifford.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:26.680
Do you know?

00:03:26.908 --> 00:03:27.788
Cuddy Hood

00:03:28.924 --> 00:03:29.844
Gryffindor!

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:38.300
It's a file of the important people who live in the technology company.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:43.060
The important people?

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.210
The boss, the client, and the company.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:47.030
If you keep that in mind, you'll be fine.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.490
You should remember this.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.430
General Clifford, the Federation's...

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:54.210
Chairman?

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:55.320
What is it?

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:58.400
William's second husband.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:03:59.880
Thank you for watching.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:00.790
Clifford.

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:01.150
What?

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:03.240
Clifford.

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:04.820
Did you understand?

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.380
What are you talking about?

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.900
Our workplace is forbidden to enter the club.

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.050
It doesn't look like a workplace.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:13.990
What?

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:18.440
What are you talking about?

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.920
The club is in the way, so get out of here.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.660
I'm sorry.

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.400
You saved me, Claire.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.180
You don't seem to want to listen to me.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:29.680
I'm sorry.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.710
I'm sorry. He and I will be working on the debris collection today.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:34.860
Is that okay?

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.360
Don't make your own decisions!

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:37.590
You're so selfish!

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.990
If you say so, I won't do it!

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:42.110
It's 120% okay!

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:42.990
Thank you.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:48.950
You're here?

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.350
Then I'll be a lawyer in the future!

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:54.610
The school is the same everywhere.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:56.930
Anyway, my father takes care of the job.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.070
In short, I wish I had a title of university.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.820
That's mine.

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:02.820
That's how it is in the world, isn't it?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.180
No, not at all.

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.180
As expected, you know it well.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.450
Come on, Tanabe-kun. Give me a cup of coffee.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:09.930
Oh, I don't need it.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:10.290
What?

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:11.570
It's cheap here, isn't it?

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:13.650
Well, this one was taken.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:14.950
Do you have cola?

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:16.610
It's not light or diet.

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:18.640
Tanabe-kun, cola.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:19.500
I don't have that.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:22.740
Oh, leave the girl alone.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.920
It's not fun to talk to an old man, is it?

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.740
Yes, then I'll go buy it.

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:29.660
Yeah, hurry up.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.160
Oh, it's me.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.990
Yes, please transfer BS-12 to the VIP gate.

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:41.990
Hey, don't just stand there.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.110
I don't have permission.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.570
I'm just going to take a look around.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.690
There shouldn't be a problem with business, though.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:48.150
I refuse.

00:05:48.670 --> 00:05:49.610
It's a business manager's order.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:52.150
Why us?

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.570
You can't say things like that to a security guard.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.700
Are you doing this for us?

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:57.780
Yeah.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.260
In other words, it's a joint business.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.540
You want me to do something good, don't you?

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:03.910
I don't want a black person with a low environmental score.

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:09.930
Hey, if you become a black person, will you make a fox room for me?

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.300
That's cramped, isn't it?

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:14.440
Let's think about it.

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:15.420
All right!

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:19.500
If you're an adult, it's over!

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:20.860
Well, that's it.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:22.970
Mr. Colin.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.480
Oh, are you leaving already?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.920
Then the rest is in the ship.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:27.500
Oh!

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:28.500
Oh, my God!

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:29.980
This Alvin D-

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.110
I've prepared a lot of things!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:33.990
Huh? I don't need it anymore.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:41.330
Well then, please be careful and make good memories!

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:44.380
See you later! Hey, Hachimaki!

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:45.700
Weren't there five employees?

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:47.020
There were six.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.910
The perfectionist and the student of social studies.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:51.950
Don't make it up.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.190
And if you're a non-profit, get a license.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:55.710
I need a license.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:56.830
Of course.

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.860
It's a shame.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:02.110
The visit is next time, so...

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:04.170
Oh, that's good, that's good. This person is good.

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:06.150
I'm listening from the boss.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.080
Your son.

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:09.620
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.200
Please confirm it with the five staff members.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:14.580
Five people?

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:19.640
Me and my seniors, Fii-san and Yuuri-san and the completionist, and...

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:21.720
What about Colin-san?

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:23.670
Well, this is the world.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.130
What is the world?

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.890
Kabe-kun!

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:28.600
Ai-chan!

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.530
Please follow me so that I don't have to work as a slave.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:38.220
There's no reason for the president to fire a private company employee.

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.520
You're about the same age as Corinne.

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:45.440
Mr. Tanabe, what are you playing with?

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:51.400
Please, I can't get a job again at this age.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:53.980
I have seven children on Earth who are hungry.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.060
Are you holding back your seniors?

00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:01.200
I copy!

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.500
I copy!

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:09.540
Yes, yes, of course, I will handle it secretly.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.210
Please leave it to me, Chairman Clifford.

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.600
In return, please take care of Debris.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:24.150
Okay, next is the salute pose.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.040
I'm sorry, it's dangerous.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:30.800
Please be careful.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.240
Hey, why don't you let me collect the debris?

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.980
Hey, this isn't a game.

00:08:36.560 --> 00:08:39.380
If you're going to play like a student, I'm going to kick you out.

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:40.620
Hey, senpai!

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:41.060
What?

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.040
He's the president's son.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:46.520
The president is too great, it has nothing to do with us debris collectors.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:47.880
It does.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:48.780
What are you going to do if you get fired?

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.600
You'll have to get a new job or have kids.

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.290
Do you have kids?

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:56.150
Anyway, I'll be soft on you, okay?

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.110
Are you done talking?

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.590
You should thank me properly.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.980
That's why, you should also...

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:02.420
Huh?

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.180
You bastard! Don't destroy someone else's ship!

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:06.040
Isn't that the usual thing?

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.300
Oh, so the new ship is his ally.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.240
An ally...

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.640
What a rotten ship.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:14.380
It's not like the one my father has.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:18.020
Eh? You have one, senpai?

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.260
The one who has a spaceship?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.680
See? You can buy one yourself.

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:25.640
Do you still have that notebook?

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:26.600
Is it bad?

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.690
Not really. It just doesn't change.

00:09:31.148 --> 00:09:31.948
Right?

00:09:31.980 --> 00:09:33.640
Isn't there a weapon on this ship?

00:09:33.676 --> 00:09:36.836
Like anti-debris missiles, or drill for demolition.

00:09:37.196 --> 00:09:39.316
There's no way there's a drill!

00:09:40.236 --> 00:09:43.196
I wonder if Hatchan and Corinne are doing well.

00:09:45.116 --> 00:09:47.376
Ravi, what have you been doing all this time?

00:09:47.376 --> 00:09:48.576
I'm doing some research!

00:09:48.684 --> 00:09:51.684
Hachiba can be used as a cashier when he has to go to work.

00:09:51.684 --> 00:09:53.784
Then, I want a soft one.

00:09:53.784 --> 00:09:55.984
You're quite old, aren't you?

00:09:56.492 --> 00:09:57.992
As expected of the captain!

00:09:57.992 --> 00:09:59.992
Then, the space cream of SEVENTEEN's specialty...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.860
It's popular. It's sold out the next day.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:11.830
Wait for your wallet. I'll wait for you.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:24.810
It's lunchtime, so I'll take you to lunch.

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:25.210
Thank you for the meal.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:35.610
Senpai.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:35.970
What?

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.940
Do you know Kuruya, the completionist?

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.560
I knew about that notebook, too.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.020
Don't stop me, Shiniri.

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:45.780
It's Tanabe.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:48.790
We're classmates.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:52.780
We only talked for about a year.

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:55.400
He's the elite of the completionists,

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:57.440
and I'm the half-baked devil.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.100
Hmm...

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:04.770
Even if you say you're a pro, it's not a big deal, is it?

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:05.240
Is that so?

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.030
I don't have a budget, so...

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:08.820
Well, it's similar everywhere.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:11.380
Huh? What a silly story.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:12.620
I just got home!

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:13.740
Oh, good job.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.400
I saw you. You're cool.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.830
Ah, thank you very much.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.200
Hey, why don't you be an instructor at your part-time job this time?

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:21.000
Huh?

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:24.610
The other day, I had a space trip with my friends, but it was messy.

00:11:25.210 --> 00:11:26.680
Eh? Only for amateurs?

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:29.980
I'm a pro for now, but...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.500
He's such an annoying and noisy old man.

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:34.080
After all, girls are better, aren't they?

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:35.150
Fee-san.

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:36.350
Are you done, Yuri?

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:39.070
Yes. I've put the whole fishbone in the container.

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.110
I'm going to turn it into a material in Seven.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:43.550
Oh, that's fine.

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:46.170
Then, all we have to do is go back to Seven.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:48.280
Change the route to 24 degrees.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:50.230
It's 35 degrees.

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:50.960
What?

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:54.130
The route is 35 degrees, please.

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:56.470
Hey, hey, what are you talking about?

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:59.030
I want to show him the communication satellite YUKAWA.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.020
I want to see you, Yukawa.

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.120
Are you telling me to stop by on my way home from work?

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:06.450
Just shifting the orbit a little bit.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:07.980
There should be no problem with the fuel or the air.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:10.440
It's not that kind of problem.

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.430
It's the director's orders.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:13.230
That again?

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:14.870
Change the route to 35 degrees.

00:12:15.550 --> 00:12:16.290
Are you serious, Bi?

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.990
The route must have been cleared.

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:19.770
Is it completed?

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:20.730
Of course.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:21.910
Yes, copy.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:23.240
Nice to meet you.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.110
Didn't you hate your parents' name, Hikari?

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:36.190
Yes, I still do.

00:12:36.530 --> 00:12:37.470
Then...

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:38.230
I want to be promoted.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:43.080
The head of the Dorf class is someone who is bound by his roots and academic background.

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:46.480
If I get a result, he will evaluate me.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:49.600
What are you going to do after you're promoted?

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:51.130
It's a waste of time.

00:12:52.060 --> 00:12:54.000
We're already over, aren't we?

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:56.620
Don't say that.

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.880
I think it's somewhere up there.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:16.790
Please zoom in on the receiver.

00:13:18.370 --> 00:13:19.270
Yes, yes.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:25.020
What is that?

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.410
It's a camera.

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.520
The latest model of the Galaxy.

00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:29.040
What?

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:29.830
The other day...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.980
I forgot to put it on when I was doing the space flight.

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:34.300
You forgot to put it on? Instructor!

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:37.480
I was so stingy like you, so I put it back on the ship first.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.580
But he's really irresponsible.

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.960
I'm an amateur, so I almost forget things.

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.380
Um, what about the delivery before the flight?

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.900
Oh, that's right. You said something.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.960
That means it's all your fault!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.030
Senpai, be a little more calm.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:53.190
Shiniri, be quiet!

00:13:53.510 --> 00:13:56.440
Even if it's a bolt size, if you make a mistake, you'll destroy the spaceship!

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.900
How serious is that!

00:13:58.900 --> 00:13:59.700
You have a bad head

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:03.950
That's why I asked you guys to pick it up secretly, right?

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:07.180
Claire! Are you going to collect the debris for this guy?

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:10.380
The Federation is an important client for our company.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:14.250
Considering the influence of his father, this is the best we can do.

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:15.530
Best we can do?

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.820
Don't say it so clearly, Claire.

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:21.150
Well, I can trust someone who knows that kind of thing.

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:24.570
Aren't you embarrassed to let your father do it?

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:29.240
Ha! That's a smart question. Think about it carefully.

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:29.380
Thank you very much.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:35.140
Those who are smart, those who have fast legs, and those who can draw and make music are all talented by their parents.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.580
Money and power are the same thing.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.420
Don't use logic. Don't rely on your parents.

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:41.760
That's not logic.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:45.490
Even if you have the power of your parents, you won't use it.

00:14:45.890 --> 00:14:47.200
It's the light of your parents.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:49.790
Don't say that. If you say that, you'll become a sun god.

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:52.210
What the hell are you talking about?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.720
Hey, I'm going out.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:59.370
Yuri, come here. Please give me the toy box.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.940
Huh, Aikobi?

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:04.360
As expected of the captain. What a wise decision.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:06.840
Tch! I've failed to look at you!

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:08.400
You're a big brother too!

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:09.510
Senpai!

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:11.030
Don't talk to a guy who's been shitting his pants since the beginning!

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:12.740
Hachi, what's that?

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:13.480
Huh?

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:14.640
Isn't that debris?

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.240
No matter who, and for what reason left it,

00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:20.960
debris doesn't change the danger.

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:21.660
And,

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:23.500
even if someone has to recover it,

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:28.560
I can't leave the debris behind.

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:29.800
Hachi!

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:31.380
What are you going to do?

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:50.300
Thank you for your hard work!

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:52.240
I'm really tired.

00:15:53.060 --> 00:15:54.970
Then, your favorite drink.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.130
And this is a boring thing, but...

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.310
To my father...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:00.400
What's that?

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.260
It's the famous 7-Eleven's space cream.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.900
We're making the cream with zero gravity, so the air should be...

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.900
Don't mess with it. Send it to your home.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.510
Oh, I didn't notice that.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:12.770
Send it to your home right away.

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:14.450
How was it, Ai-chan?

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:15.330
Did Hachi stay quiet?

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.260
Well...

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.250
Well, somehow...

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:20.410
Clear!

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.570
I'm sorry, class president!

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.670
We safely finished all the missions and returned.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.140
Good work.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:27.840
Go home, Koryu-san.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:28.740
I was saved.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.180
I'll keep it to myself.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:32.650
Thank you very much.

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:37.100
I've been waiting for you at the block of my car.

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:38.730
Welcome back.

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:44.250
I'm glad you came to pick me up.

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:48.630
No, I put a new sofa in my cruiser.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:51.070
By the way, what is it?

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.100
Hey, is my camera okay?

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:55.290
Yeah, it's fine.

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:59.470
I checked the radiation, but there's no problem at all.

00:16:59.470 --> 00:16:59.690
Thank you for watching.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.110
Hey, why don't we do fireworks at Hakoba Kido this time?

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:09.770
We can get something we can do in space with the back route.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:11.230
Hey!

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:12.300
Are you saying we can date them?

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:15.420
Captain, how long are they going to stay?

00:17:15.540 --> 00:17:16.400
I'm going to cry!

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:17.300
I'm going to cry!

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:18.480
Let's get rid of the bad guys.

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:20.430
It's okay.

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:23.230
We'll get them back at that time.

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:24.980
I don't have any cash.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:26.760
Thanks to the bad guys,

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.020
these people can live on.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.980
If you don't give me a job, I'll be a volunteer devil.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:34.100
Hahaha!

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:35.480
You bastard!

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:36.740
Senpai!

00:17:36.900 --> 00:17:37.180
Hachi!

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:37.960
Stop it!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:38.940
I'm a member of the Federation!

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:41.250
Hoshido-kun!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.470
You should understand your position!

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:44.820
Don't you have any pride?

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:49.080
Senpai!

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:50.320
Doshiri!

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:53.200
So? What are you going to do from here?

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:54.500
I'll go to the Federation Police!

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:56.240
Ehh?

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:58.570
The evidence of the devil is a crime.

00:17:58.570 --> 00:17:58.770
I don't know what I'm talking about.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.000
It's useless.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.460
It's really bad for you.

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:05.870
Your father has a good reputation in the police force.

00:18:07.130 --> 00:18:10.190
Besides, according to the record, I'm not on the ship, right?

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:11.790
You can't win even if you sue me.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:14.910
Don't think that you can be free because your father is great!

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:17.270
Then, if you like to hit or kick me,

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.830
your job will be gone.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:23.800
Oh, or do you want to quit?

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:27.300
It's a secret to your parents that you pick up garbage in space.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:28.360
Huh?

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:29.950
Oh, that's...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:36.050
Every single day, every single day, I have to do a lot of work.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:39.490
Do you really want to cling to the universe that much?

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:40.750
That's disgusting.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:43.280
Why don't you introduce me to your job?

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:47.160
At this rate, you guys will really become the garbage of the universe.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.680
You bastard!

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:50.680
What?

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.780
You...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.000
I'm going to throw it away. I'm going to put it on my head.

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.220
What do you mean you don't understand?

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:05.860
Debris are the coolest.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:07.690
It makes the universe safe.

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:08.690
It protects the planet.

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:11.320
It's the power of the universe.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:16.200
The person who only talks about his father is the garbage of the universe.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:22.380
Stop it, Ai-chan.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:23.100
He's the son of the federal secretary.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.880
Hey, Bom-bom. Remember.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.970
We're not picking up debris for you.

00:19:30.920 --> 00:19:32.020
What are you going to do, Korin?

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:34.280
Show me your cool side!

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:37.960
D-Dolph-san, what do you think about this as a Technola company?

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:42.050
This is a violent incident against an outsider, isn't it?

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:43.050
I'm really sorry.

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:44.830
Let's get rid of it as soon as possible.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:45.570
Was it an incident?

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:47.960
What are you talking about?

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:49.210
Um...

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:50.150
That's right.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:51.390
There should have been nothing.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.210
Business manager.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:55.840
According to the record, there are only people in our company here.

00:19:56.200 --> 00:19:59.900
Therefore, violence against outsiders is not...

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.280
Oh, so that's how it is?

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:04.260
Do not joke!

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.100
Oh! Hey!!

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:08.280
Oh!!

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:08.520
Oh!!

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:20.180
That time, I'll make a statement of you all!

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.950
I'm a coward?!

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:23.430
Oh!

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.180
No, no, no!

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.200
Soon, Techno-Rusher Office Block.

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:37.750
I'm sorry for the inconvenience.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:39.490
Please tell the chairman as well.

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:41.490
No, I was saved.

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:43.160
Thank you very much.

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:43.620
What?

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:44.420
Where are everyone?

00:20:44.760 --> 00:20:45.950
Everyone was able to take a break.

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:47.250
What?

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:48.810
What is that?

00:20:49.090 --> 00:20:50.920
Then, we will do this.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:52.000
Remember.

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:55.360
Techno-Rusher is easy to get out of space.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.660
That's it, Obocchama.

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.390
If you want to say more,

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.700
You have no choice but to do it yourself.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.170
Think of it as a good lesson and do your best.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:07.470
Or is it better to report everything to your father?

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:13.420
I'm not sorry.

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:15.660
If I'm in the way...

00:21:15.780 --> 00:21:16.480
Apologize.

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.860
I'll work on it and pay you back.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:22.150
What about Hachirota's punishment?

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:26.190
Chief Clifford is a person who can't calculate, unlike his son.

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:27.010
Huh?

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:28.450
Rather than getting his employees punished,

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:28.830
Thank you for watching.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.320
It would be better if you didn't have a relationship with me.

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:33.620
You think so, don't you?

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:34.920
How is it?

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:38.710
I'm so depressed.

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:40.730
I've already given up on the kitchen.

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:44.930
It's not like you're going to treat me like a criminal now.

00:21:45.850 --> 00:21:46.630
I'm sorry.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.520
Why can't I stand it?

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:50.870
It's a request!

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:52.740
The原爆組 is a request!

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:54.580
And I'm going to have you forgive me!

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:55.180
What?

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:58.440
At times like this, ordinary people take responsibility.

00:21:58.860 --> 00:21:59.460
I see.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:21:59.960
D.O.R.G.A.R.

00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:01.140
Senjo?

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:01.520
Chief!

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:02.270
Chief!

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:04.310
What? Why me?

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:07.370
I'm the highest-ranking officer, so I'm here to help!

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:08.960
Um, what about the constitution?

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:11.820
Oh, that's fine! No bonuses for everyone!

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:14.200
No way! I can't pay for the childcare!

00:22:15.260 --> 00:22:16.540
I don't care anymore.

00:22:16.720 --> 00:22:17.280
Why don't you go eat?

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:18.840
Yeah!

00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:20.910
That's right. I'm done with work.

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:21.990
Hey, Hikun!

00:22:22.310 --> 00:22:23.750
I'll leave the rest to you and the chief.

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:25.450
All right! I'm here!

00:22:25.670 --> 00:22:26.570
Hey, what are you doing?

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:27.930
It's been a long time since I went to eat at the general block!

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:29.750
Yuuri is coming!

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.900
Of course. Let's go to a luxurious place today.

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:35.680
Is it the constitution?

00:22:36.180 --> 00:22:36.740
Yes.

00:22:38.190 --> 00:22:40.180
Hey, Tanabe, come here.

00:22:40.400 --> 00:22:43.450
The food in the general block is a little expensive, but it's delicious.

00:22:43.830 --> 00:22:45.670
You haven't been there yet, have you?

00:22:46.090 --> 00:22:46.650
Tanabe.

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:55.620
I'm going to eat it with your pension.

00:22:56.760 --> 00:22:57.320
What?

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:00.140
Hahahaha

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:24.110
Hoshimi ga uo

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:42.140
Even if you get drunk and faint, you'll always be drunk

00:24:07.610 --> 00:24:07.970
I don't know.

00:24:34.800 --> 00:24:36.930
I even gave it a name.

00:24:37.330 --> 00:24:40.550
So this isn't a space ship, it's a life-saving ball.

00:24:41.140 --> 00:24:42.510
Cut! Cut!

00:24:42.750 --> 00:24:44.430
So you decided to die in space?

00:24:45.270 --> 00:24:47.470
Well, there aren't many kind people in the world.

00:24:48.030 --> 00:24:48.640
Gah!

00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:53.290
I'm going to kill you, but I can't do this!

00:24:54.860 --> 00:24:57.230
Even if you do that, you can't escape anywhere!
